export const GUIDE = "- Tell us about your truck: Tap Truck. Enter how tall, heavy, and long it is. Then we keep you away from low bridges and roads trucks can't use.\n- Pick where to go: Tap here and type an address or a company name. Then tap Start. The phone tells you every turn out loud.\n- Route: your trip: Tap Route to see your way there, how long it takes, tolls and fuel stops. You can save maps here for places with no signal.\n- Faster route: Switch or Keep: If traffic builds up, RigRoute tells you about a faster truck-safe road. Tap Switch to take it or Keep to stay. It never changes your route by itself.\n- HOS: your driving clock: Tap HOS to see how many hours you can still drive today and when your break is due. It is a helper, not your legal log.\n- Load: your job: Tap Load for your pickup, drop-off, times and papers like the BOL. Loads your dispatcher sends you show up here.\n- Warn other drivers: See a crash, police, or road work? Tap here. Other drivers will see it on their map.\n- Me: you and your settings: Tap Me for your points, friends, language and voice. No account needed: your settings stay on this phone. Something broken or have an idea? Use Report a Bug / Suggestion there.\n- Help RigRoute grow: In Me you can choose to share your city and state, never your exact spot. It is off unless you turn it on.\n- Report a Bug / Suggestion: In Me, open Report a Bug / Suggestion. Say what went wrong or what to add. You can add a screenshot.\n- Email us: In Me, under Report a Bug, tap Email us to write to the RigRoute team.\n- Need help?: Tap ? on any screen. It tells you what the screen does, and it can read it out loud. You can also type a question or tap Show me around.\n- Add a stop: Pick where to go first. Tap Route, then tap + Add stop. Type the address or city and tap ＋ Add stop. RigRoute plans the trip through your stop. For many stops, tap 🗺 Stops at the bottom to make a Multi-stop route.\n- Set your rig size: Tap 🚛 Truck at the bottom. Pick your vehicle type, then enter height, weight, length and axles. Tap Save. Every route is then checked for low bridges, weight limits and roads trucks cannot use.\n- Speed limit: The speed limit sign shows the posted limit for your road. If the road has no posted sign in our map, it shows a normal limit for that state and road with est. next to it. RigRoute only warns you about speeding when the limit is posted.\n- Hazmat and scales: In Route, tap ☣ Hazmat: off to turn hazmat on, so tunnels and roads that ban hazmat are skipped. Tap ⚖️ Avoid scales to stay off weigh station roads when you can.\n- Use the HOS clock: Tap ⏱ HOS. Tap Off duty, Sleeper, On duty or Driving when you change. It shows drive time left, your 14-hour window, when your 30-minute break is due, and your 70-hour cycle. It is not an ELD.\n- Get loads from dispatch: Tap 📋 Loads at the top. Type your name and the Dispatcher code your dispatcher gave you, then connect. New loads show up there. Tap a load to see stops, then Navigate to pickup or Navigate to delivery.\n- Report a hazard: Tap 📣 Report. Pick what you see, like Police, Hazard, Road closed or Low clearance. It is marked on the road just ahead of you and shared with other drivers. Pins go away by themselves after a few hours.\n- Is that pin still there?: Tap a hazard pin on the map. Tap 👍 Still there if you see it, or 👎 Not there if it is gone. You cannot vote on your own pin. You get one vote per pin.\n- Friends: Tap 👥 Friends at the top. Share your friend code or QR with a friend. When a friend is added, RigRoute asks: Share my location with them? Not now is the default. Nothing is shared until you tap Yes, and you can turn it off any time in Friends.\n- Find truck parking and fuel: Plan a route, then tap ⛽ on the map to see truck stops, rest areas, parking and weigh stations ahead. If your hours run short, HOS shows the last truck parking before your clock runs out.\n- Voice and language: Tap 😎 Me. Under 🌐 Language pick your language. Use ▶ Preview voice to hear the voice. Turn spoken turns on or off there too.\n- Use with no signal: Plan your route, then in Route tap ⬇ Save route map for offline. The map and route then work where there is no signal.\n- What's new: Tap 😎 Me and open 🆕 What's new to see the latest changes.\n- Your privacy and data: There are no accounts. Your settings stay on this phone. In Me, open Privacy to Export my data or Delete all data. Help RigRoute grow is off unless you turn it on.\n- Start and end a trip: Tap Where to? and pick a place. Tap ▶ Start navigation. Tap End to stop. Demo drive shows the trip without driving.";
